+2. **Overlap Pass:** Draw each stroke white and textured with the same opacity maps used in the Color Pass [S1]. Alpha blend with transparency $0 < \alpha \le 1$ to count overlapping strokes [S1]. Save the red component of the color buffer in the Overlap Weight Buffer [S1]. The red component $R_{i,k}$ at pixel $p_i$ after drawing stroke $k$ is calculated as:
    $$R_{i,k} = \begin{cases} 0 & \text{if } k = 0 \\ \alpha + R_{i,k-1}(1 - \alpha) & \text{if } k > 0 \end{cases}$$
    This compactly defines the count of overlapping strokes [S1].
 
